\.TH REGRET 1 "2026-09-26" "Bad Decisions Client 1.8.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
regret \- deal rounds from a Bad Decisions API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B regret
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B regret deal
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B regret health
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B regret feedback
.RI {enjoy|regret|clear} [ options ]
.br
.B regret provenance
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B regret identity
.RI {status|reset|off|on}
.br
.B regret consequences
.RI {status|enjoy|regret|enable|disable}
.br
.B regret together
.RI room " [--name display-name] [--api-url url] [--heartbeat seconds]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B regret
is the dependency-light terminal client for a Bad Decisions service. It deals rounds, lists packs, checks health, records optional feedback, and prints provenance from the last local draw.
.PP
Consequences is opt-in. It controls both voting and the pseudonymous telemetry required for voting. Non-interactive use leaves it disabled unless an explicit preference is already stored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --api-url url
Use a compatible API endpoint. The default is https://bytes.coffee/bad-decisions.
.TP
.BI --packs ids
Comma-separated pack IDs for both colors.
.TP
.BI --black-packs ids
Override the black-card selector.
.TP
.BI --white-packs ids
Override the white-card selector.
.TP
.BR --list-packs
List packs from the service.
.TP
.BR --health
Check service health.
.TP
.BR --json
Print machine-readable JSON where supported.
.TP
.BI --timeout seconds
Network timeout. Must be greater than zero.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI deal
Deal and print one round. This is the default command.
.TP
.BI health
Check the API health endpoint.
.TP
.BI feedback enjoy|regret|clear
Submit, change, or withdraw the last eligible vote. Requires Enjoy Consequences.
.TP
.BI provenance [--json]
Print license, attribution, version, and source metadata for packs in the last saved draw without contacting the API.
.TP
.BI identity status|reset|off|on
Inspect, rotate, omit, or restore the local pseudonymous installation identity. Identity use is still subordinate to Consequences consent.
.TP
.BI consequences status
Show whether Consequences is enabled.
.TP
.BI consequences enjoy
Enable voting and stable-ID pseudonymous vote telemetry.
.TP
.BI consequences regret
Disable voting and vote telemetry entirely.
.TP
.BI together room
Join or reconnect to an ephemeral Peer Pressure multiplayer room. The first participant is the initial Responsible Adult. The client maintains authenticated heartbeats, submits private responses, and resynchronizes stale room state automatically. Use --name when no saved room session exists.
.SH CONSENT
On the first interactive deal, an unset or stale consent preference prompts once. Choose Enjoy Consequences or Regret Consequences. The choice and consent schema version are stored locally and survive upgrades. Pressing Enter chooses regret. Non-interactive invocations never block for consent.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.regret.env
Atomic local preferences and pseudonymous identity state.
.TP
.I ~/.regret-last-round.json
The last draw's provenance and, when eligible, its feedback capability.
.TP
.I ~/.regret-peer-pressure.json
Protected room-local player IDs and reconnect capabilities. Written atomically with mode 0600. These identities are independent of Consequences.
.SH PRIVACY
No account is required. A stable pseudonymous identifier is used only when Consequences is enabled. Disabling Consequences disables voting and its telemetry. The client does not use this identifier for update checks or Peer Pressure; version checks are cached and use the configured API health endpoint. Peer Pressure sends only the authenticated room-local identity and state needed for gameplay.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Network, configuration, or unavailable-feedback failure.
